aufs-ng (0~git20260807.842ab15-1minios3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix boot failure when a plain ext4 filesystem root is used as an AUFS
    branch, including DynFileFS persistence containers.
  * Keep other revalidation callbacks, encrypted names and casefold roots
    outside the exception.
  * Add VM regression coverage for ext4 root branches, copy-up, whiteouts,
    dynamic branch changes and rejected revalidating/casefold roots.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 01:39:27 +0300

aufs-ng (0~git20260807.842ab15-1minios2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Allow dynamic branch removal to converge duplicate pinned directory
    generations created when inotify keeps an inode alive after its dentry is
    reclaimed.
  * Keep the hardlink collision guard unchanged for non-directory inodes.
  * Add a UML regression for two inotify-pinned directory generations across
    dynamic branch add/remove.
  * Package MiniOS source changes as quilt patches against the pristine
    upstream snapshot.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 20:39:20 +0300

aufs-ng (0~git20260807.842ab15-1minios1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial MiniOS DKMS package.
  * Backport aufs-ng to Linux 6.12 while retaining support for newer kernels.
  * Handle both backing_file_open() ABIs found in the Linux 6.12 stable series.
  * Verify the compatibility layer with the upstream 128-test UML suite on
    Linux 6.12.94 and 6.12.105 with lockdep, RCU checks and panic_on_warn.

